## 1. XPT2046 SPI Driver [CYD-TOUCH-DRIVER]

### 1.1 SPI Device Registration [CYD-TOUCH-SPI]

Add XPT2046 as second device on `SPI2_HOST` (shared with ILI9341 display). The SPI bus is already initialized by `ILI9341::init_spi()`.

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Host | `SPI2_HOST` (same as display) |
| CS | GPIO 33 (`CYD_TOUCH_CS`) |
| Clock | 2.5 MHz (`CYD_SPI_TOUCH_FREQ_HZ`) |
| SPI Mode | 0 |
| Queue size | 1 |

The driver exposes a `spi_device_handle_t` for touch transactions. The display already holds its own handle from `spi_bus_add_device`. Both devices share the bus — ESP-IDF's SPI master driver handles CS arbitration.

### 1.2 Touch Read Protocol [CYD-TOUCH-READ]

XPT2046 command bytes:

| Channel | Command byte | Notes |
|---------|-------------|-------|
| X position | `0xD0` | 12-bit ADC, differential mode |
| Y position | `0x90` | 12-bit ADC, differential mode |
| Z1 pressure | `0xB0` | For touch-down detection |
| Z2 pressure | `0xC0` | For touch-down detection |

Read sequence per sample:
1. Send command byte, read 2 bytes (12-bit result in bits 11:0, MSB first)
2. Take 3 samples per axis, use median (reject noise)
3. Compute pressure: `z = z1 > 0 ? (x_raw * (z2/z1 - 1)) : 0`

Files: `src/touch_xpt2046.cpp`, `include/touch_xpt2046.h`

```cpp
struct TouchReading {
    uint16_t raw_x;     // 0-4095
    uint16_t raw_y;     // 0-4095
    uint16_t pressure;  // 0 = no touch
    bool touched;       // pressure > threshold
};

class XPT2046 {
public:
    void init();  // spi_bus_add_device on SPI2_HOST
    TouchReading read();  // median-of-3 raw reading
};
```

### 1.3 Bus Sequencing [CYD-TOUCH-SEQUENCE]

Touch reads and display DMA transfers share HSPI. ESP-IDF's SPI master driver serializes transactions by device handle, so explicit mutex is not required. However, touch reads must not occur during `render_frame()` band DMA. The sequencing:

```
while (true) {
    touch = xpt2046.read();           // SPI touch transaction
    process_touch(touch);              // hit test + dispatch
    canvas.render_frame(draw_scene);   // 20 band DMA transactions
    vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(10));
}
```

Touch read happens **before** `render_frame()` in each loop iteration. No concurrent access.

> **CORRECTED 2026-08-14 — the sketch above is the Phase 1c loop and is retained only as
> the sequencing rationale; it is not the loop that exists.** Two claims need qualifying:
>
> - **The ordering claim still holds.** Touch is still sampled before the render step in
>   each pass, now as a burst — `main.cpp:675-682` (poll) precedes `:694-727` (render).
> - **"Explicit mutex is not required" is no longer true.** ESP-IDF still serializes by
>   device handle, but the loop is no longer the only renderer: the HTTP capture server
>   pull-renders on its own task, sharing the band buffer and the SPI bus. The whole loop
>   body therefore runs under an explicit render lock, `capture_http_lock()` /
>   `capture_http_unlock()` (`main.cpp:662,729`; declared `capture_http.h:35-36`, taken by
>   the server at `capture_http.cpp:139,181`), and the scene-swap path takes it separately
>   (`main.cpp:750,756`).
>
> The real loop is described in §5.3. Drift baseline:
> `[DEC-SPEC-DRIFT-BASELINE-CYD-2026-08]`.

