## 4. Hit Testing and Widget Dispatch [CYD-TOUCH-HIT]

### 4.1 Widget Registry [CYD-TOUCH-REGISTRY]

The scene callback already draws widgets at known Rects. A static registry maps widgets to their layout rects for hit testing:

```cpp
struct WidgetEntry {
    Widget* widget;
    Rect rect;
};

static constexpr int kMaxWidgets = 16;
static WidgetEntry widget_registry[kMaxWidgets];
static int widget_count = 0;

void register_widget(Widget* w, const Rect& r);
void clear_registry();
```

The registry is a flat array. **`kMaxWidgets` is 32, not the 16 this section originally
stated** (`touch_dispatch.h:25`; corrected 2026-08-14 — the limit was raised as scenes grew,
and a stale "16 entries max" comment survives at `touch_dispatch.cpp:7`, which is a code
comment defect, not a spec one). Overflow is handled by refusing the registration with a
warning naming the widget, never by overrunning (`touch_dispatch.cpp:32-36`).

`register_widget()` is not called by hand. Registration is derived from the scene by
`scene_register_touch()` and re-derived when visibility flips or the scene is swapped — see
§5.2 for the three call sites.

### 4.2 Hit Test [CYD-TOUCH-HITTEST]

On TAP event:

```cpp
Widget* hit_test(float sx, float sy) {
    // Reverse order: last registered = topmost (z-order)
    for (int i = widget_count - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        Rect& r = widget_registry[i].rect;
        if (sx >= r.x && sx < r.x + r.w &&
            sy >= r.y && sy < r.y + r.h) {
            return widget_registry[i].widget;
        }
    }
    return nullptr;
}
```

### 4.3 Widget Dispatch [CYD-TOUCH-DISPATCH]

When hit test finds a widget, call `widget->on_tap(local_x, local_y)` where local coordinates are relative to the widget's Rect origin:

```cpp
local_x = screen_x - widget_rect.x;
local_y = screen_y - widget_rect.y;
widget->on_tap(local_x, local_y);
```

### 4.4 Widget on_tap Implementations [CYD-TOUCH-WIDGET-TAP]

Override `on_tap()` in existing widgets for Phase 1c demo:

| Widget | on_tap Behavior |
|--------|----------------|
| GaugeWidget | Set value to tapped position mapped to min/max range. Tap left side = lower, right side = higher. |
| LEDWidget | Toggle state: Off→On, On→Off, Warning→Off, Danger→Off |
| LabelWidget | No action (labels are not interactive) |
| RectangleWidget | No action |

